>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The atom inventory identifies the two-coordinate carbene carbon of IMes and two diester skeletons without olefinic hydrogen. The donor limiting form contains two neutral dimethyl acetylenedicarboxylate ligands, one neutral NHC and Pd(0). Coordination lowers the calculated order of the carbon–carbon multiple bonds. The hydrogen evidence records the discrepancy between the H36 CIF model and the fumarate name in the paper. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

